  "bodyText": "Home\nVisit Us\nExhibitions\nEvents\nOnline Talks\nOxfordshire’s Military Heritage in 50 Objects\nCollections\nBlog\nResearch\nLearning\nShop\nCart\nMy Account\nAbout\nBecome a Friend\nSupport Us\nRoom Hire\n\n01993 810 210\n\nfrontofhouse@sofo.org.uk\n\n  \nHome\nEvents\nExhibitions\nCollections\nFriends’ Membership\nVisit\nShop\nBasket\nMy Account\nOxfordshire’s Military Heritage in 50 Objects\nResearch\nLearning\nOnline Talks\nBlog\nSupport Us\nRoom Hire\nImage Services\nAbout\nOUR GALLERIES & EXHIBITIONS\nTemporary Exhibitions\nThe Cloister Gallery (Ground Floor)\n\nThe Briefing Room Gallery (Ground Floor)\n\nThe Landing Gallery (First Floor)\n\n \n\nThe Main Gallery\n\nYou'll find Oxfordshire county and regimental timelines at the entrance to our Main Gallery, but once you enter you'll find a series of self-contained 'pods' which cover a diverse range of stories, topics and themes.\n\nOur Permanent Displays\n\nWinston Churchill and The Queens Own Oxfordshire Hussars\n\nSecret Agents, Secret Armies\n\nPrisoners of War at Home and Abroad\n\nThe Liberation of Bergen Belsen by the Oxfordshire Yeomanry\n\nGlobal Army: From the Age of Empire to the Modern Day\n\nBloody Battles & Dangerous Diseases\n\nBattles: The Oxfordshire and Buckinghamshire Light Infantry in the Second World War\n\nA Woman's War: Domestic and Fighting Fronts \n\nOur County, Our War: Remembering the Great War\n\nArt Submissions\n\nWe accept art exhibition submissions on an ongoing basis.\n\nThe museum looks at artistic vision and merit, relevance to our audiences, diversity, and budget when considering any proposal.\n\nIndividual artists and curators working in any media or discipline are welcome to apply.\n\nExhibitions may be selected from submitted proposals as well from those initiated by the museum team.\n\nPlease contact Ursula Corcoran at the museum for an initial discussion, or email your proposal to:\n\nmuseumdirector@sofo.org.uk\n\nOther Permanent Displays\n\nOther permanent displays you'll find outside of our Main Gallery\n\n \n\nSoldiers of Oxfordshire Museum\nPark Street.\nWoodstock\nOxfordshire OX20 1SN\n\nPhone and Email:\nGeneral Enquiries & Event Tickets: 01993 810 211\nfrontofhouse@sofo.org.uk\n\nPrivacy Policy\nTerms and conditions",
